warning[SC0414]: this stores `x` where code outside this function may read it, and it may point to a freed allocation
    ╭─[ a_freed_pointer_copied_into_a_local_a_call_kept_is_reported.c:13:5 ]
    │
  8 │     int *x = malloc(4);
    │              ────┬────  
    │                  ╰────── allocated here
    │ 
 12 │     free(x);
    │     ───┬───  
    │        ╰───── freed here
 13 │     memcpy(&slot, &x, 8);
    │     ──────────┬─────────  
    │               ╰─────────── stored here, where it may have been freed before
────╯
  = note: this check belongs to safety level 1
  = note: this could not be proven; it is an error without `--allow-unknown`
  = help: if it is freed, free it on every path or on none, and keep it out of a call this check cannot read in between
